  "problem": "Determine the graph of the following parametrically defined curve:\n\n$$\nx=2t,\\,\\,\\,y=\\frac{5}{t},\\,t>0\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "We need to create a table of values and then sketch the curve. First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x=2t.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $0.5$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ | $10$ |\n| $y$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y=\\frac{5}{t}.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $0.5$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ | $10$ |\n| $y$ | $10$ | $5$ | $2.5$ | $1.67$ | $1.25$ | $1$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948638/assets/9707a9d11909ba22a0b90dc3e65aaa0c1bba657cbe42006719b55d4a937573f5.png)",
